{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on fb6ea164: a StateView is supported for its interface only.\n\n1. The supported observation of given.view is a call of a method that\n   the StateView interface declares. The container's own keys, its\n   prototype, its constructor and each member outside the interface\n   are outside the supported observation.\n2. This boundary exists before E1. The runtime judges on SqliteStore,\n   and the verifier and the tests judge on MemoryState. The two have\n   different own members today. A rule that read one would give the\n   runtime and the replay different answers and break promise 9. So\n   E1 preserves no backend shape for the container, and it adds no\n   key filter and no unavailable answer for it.\n3. The exact key list of 654ec50a covers the Given and the data that\n   a rule reads from it: intent, fields, from, fromItems, rows,\n   records and snapshots. It does not cover the view container.\n4. Review obligation, as in a870c343: state in the checkpoint, from a\n   source search, that no capability rule and no platform rule\n   enumerates given.view, reads a member outside the StateView\n   interface, or reads its prototype or constructor. List each site\n   if one exists.\n\nI add this boundary to section 5.4 with the port rule.\n\nNF-6: the source inventory 9e829765 is noted. Its implementation\nwaits for the NF-5 landing, as you state.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}